WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.903 --> 00:00:04.916
- What's up Believe Nation it's Evan.

00:00:04.916 --> 00:00:07.341
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:07.341 --> 00:00:09.183
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:12.164
And my sincere hope is
that if you see in you

00:00:12.164 --> 00:00:15.889
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:18.335
So to help you on your journey
today I'm going to talk about

00:00:18.335 --> 00:00:21.168
seven ways to be more disciplined.

00:00:25.638 --> 00:00:28.305
(hip hop music)

00:00:29.243 --> 00:00:31.239
So staying disciplined, staying focused,

00:00:31.239 --> 00:00:33.750
staying on task is one of the
hardest things for especially

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.370
creative entrepreneurs
to do because we have all

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:37.660
these things that we want
to do when we're in our head

00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:39.146
and dreaming and envisioning.

00:00:39.146 --> 00:00:41.163
But then we actually have to do the work

00:00:41.163 --> 00:00:42.248
and be disciplined about it.

00:00:42.248 --> 00:00:44.154
So I thought I'd share
with you my seven tips

00:00:44.154 --> 00:00:46.904
on how to be successful doing it.

00:00:49.107 --> 00:00:51.236
Tip number one is create
a morning routine.

00:00:51.236 --> 00:00:52.783
You have to start off right.

00:00:52.783 --> 00:00:54.752
So many times it happens
with entrepreneurs

00:00:54.752 --> 00:00:57.399
and it happened to me
so many multiple times,

00:00:57.399 --> 00:00:58.969
you get inspired randomly.

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:01.178
I would get inspired randomly.

00:01:01.178 --> 00:01:03.299
I would meet somebody at
for coffee and we'd be

00:01:03.299 --> 00:01:04.940
bubbling ideas and I get so inspired

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.603
and go home and work.

00:01:06.603 --> 00:01:09.246
Or listen to a YouTube video
or read a book or something

00:01:09.246 --> 00:01:10.992
that would just fire me up.

00:01:10.992 --> 00:01:13.482
And I'd be working like
crazy and then the next day

00:01:13.482 --> 00:01:15.952
we'll wake up and like
poof, it's like it's gone.

00:01:15.952 --> 00:01:17.725
I'm starting over from scratch.

00:01:17.725 --> 00:01:19.845
I felt like I start over from scratch

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.031
and I still do, I feel
like I start from scratch

00:01:22.031 --> 00:01:23.355
every single day.

00:01:23.355 --> 00:01:26.058
The baseline becomes
maybe a little bit higher

00:01:26.058 --> 00:01:29.094
over time, but I'm still
starting off from scratch.

00:01:29.094 --> 00:01:31.273
I don't wake up energized, passionate,

00:01:31.273 --> 00:01:33.299
ready to go attack the day.

00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:35.657
You know ,that's not me
at least maybe that's you,

00:01:35.657 --> 00:01:37.435
maybe that's some people if
that's you you're probably

00:01:37.435 --> 00:01:38.358
watching this video.

00:01:38.358 --> 00:01:41.479
But I think most people wake
up starting from scratch.

00:01:41.479 --> 00:01:43.854
I think we put on this
entrepreneur mask of like yeah

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:45.956
I'm hosting hard I'm
grinding but we wake up

00:01:45.956 --> 00:01:47.353
and we're not we're not grinding,

00:01:47.353 --> 00:01:49.466
we're not we're not super motivated.

00:01:49.466 --> 00:01:51.523
It doesn't mean we hate
our life but we know

00:01:51.523 --> 00:01:53.037
we could be working harder.

00:01:53.037 --> 00:01:54.606
I think you need a daily reset

00:01:54.606 --> 00:01:56.617
and it's figuring out what is
the one thing that gets you

00:01:56.617 --> 00:01:59.002
inspired, that gets you passionate,
that gets you motivated.

00:01:59.002 --> 00:02:02.542
To get you, it's like I want
to go do something today.

00:02:02.542 --> 00:02:05.083
You've all felt that feeling before.

00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.747
I know the way it is for
me, a lot of times it's it's

00:02:07.747 --> 00:02:12.131
the videos it's watching
successful people having success.

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.121
But that's what I want to do

00:02:14.121 --> 00:02:18.180
and seeing it on a regular
basis makes me want to do it.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:20.966
So I made the channel
selfishly for myself too,

00:02:20.966 --> 00:02:23.623
like the top ten, they're meant
for me, all those is for me.

00:02:23.623 --> 00:02:25.604
I want to see, it I want
to get motivated, I want

00:02:25.604 --> 00:02:28.160
to be inspired, I want
to learn knowledge yes.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.425
But just seeing people doing great things

00:02:30.425 --> 00:02:32.102
makes me want to do great things.

00:02:32.102 --> 00:02:34.841
so that's what helps me,
so start your day with it.

00:02:34.841 --> 00:02:37.064
It's why I did the Enspresso
Series, like start your day

00:02:37.064 --> 00:02:40.754
with a shot of an
enspresso to get you going.

00:02:40.754 --> 00:02:43.440
But if that's not your thing, it's cool.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.134
You don't have to watch
my channel, I get it.

00:02:45.134 --> 00:02:47.848
Read a book, meet with a friend,

00:02:47.848 --> 00:02:49.482
listen to a podcast.

00:02:49.482 --> 00:02:52.263
Whatever the thing is
there's no judgment you know

00:02:52.263 --> 00:02:55.304
like playing with your
ring gets you excited

00:02:55.304 --> 00:02:57.298
or waxing your eyebrows
or whatever it is like

00:02:57.298 --> 00:02:58.619
it doesn't matter.

00:02:58.619 --> 00:03:01.426
Whatever the thing is
that gets you like rah,

00:03:01.426 --> 00:03:03.843
this day is going to be
great, do that every day.

00:03:03.843 --> 00:03:07.381
Start your day with it because
if you start your day off

00:03:07.381 --> 00:03:09.469
on the wrong foot or
you start your day off

00:03:09.469 --> 00:03:13.633
just falling into your schedule
you may not be inspired

00:03:13.633 --> 00:03:15.334
the whole day.

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:17.117
Or you may randomly come across something

00:03:17.117 --> 00:03:18.444
at four o'clock that day

00:03:18.444 --> 00:03:20.459
and then that's what
gets you all motivated

00:03:20.459 --> 00:03:22.446
but you've lost from when
you wake up tp four o'clock.

00:03:22.446 --> 00:03:24.388
Right, there's a lot of time
in there that could have

00:03:24.388 --> 00:03:26.289
been way more productive
focusing on important things.

00:03:26.289 --> 00:03:28.896
And so find the thing
that gets you motivated,

00:03:28.896 --> 00:03:30.581
that gets you energized
and start your day with it

00:03:30.581 --> 00:03:31.998
every single day.

00:03:34.362 --> 00:03:36.555
Tip number two is create
a regular schedule.

00:03:36.555 --> 00:03:38.502
I think it's way easier
to be disciplined when you

00:03:38.502 --> 00:03:40.574
have a schedule that you are following.

00:03:40.574 --> 00:03:42.917
One of the hardest things
I think for entrepreneurs

00:03:42.917 --> 00:03:45.453
is we have to balance this thing

00:03:45.453 --> 00:03:46.972
if we want creative freedom,

00:03:46.972 --> 00:03:48.685
we want creative expression,
we want to be able

00:03:48.685 --> 00:03:49.965
to do what we want to do.

00:03:49.965 --> 00:03:52.437
But also we need to have
some kind of routine,

00:03:52.437 --> 00:03:54.944
some kind of discipline
because left to our own means

00:03:54.944 --> 00:03:57.614
we may not wake up and
do anything on that day

00:03:57.614 --> 00:03:59.855
or at least anything
of substance or values.

00:03:59.855 --> 00:04:01.551
It's easy to get
distracted by other things

00:04:01.551 --> 00:04:03.479
and it's not furthering our goals.

00:04:03.479 --> 00:04:05.994
And so what I find really helps for me is

00:04:05.994 --> 00:04:07.688
I create a regular schedule

00:04:07.688 --> 00:04:09.894
and every day I kind
of know what I'm doing.

00:04:09.894 --> 00:04:11.569
And I chunk my time some
Mondays are one thing

00:04:11.569 --> 00:04:13.276
and Tuesday's another thing

00:04:13.276 --> 00:04:14.938
and Wedenesday's another thing and so on

00:04:14.938 --> 00:04:16.656
for the rest of the week.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.836
And when I wake up on a
Monday morning I don't have to

00:04:18.836 --> 00:04:20.566
think about what I'm doing today .

00:04:20.566 --> 00:04:22.494
It's already there, it's on my list.

00:04:22.494 --> 00:04:25.188
I have my tasks I know
what I'm doing Monday.

00:04:25.188 --> 00:04:27.329
I start with a great morning ritual

00:04:27.329 --> 00:04:29.094
and then I'm into my day.

00:04:29.094 --> 00:04:30.144
Right.

00:04:30.144 --> 00:04:32.120
And I think that helps most of the time.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.334
I think on the rare occasion
that you feel inspired by

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.386
something else like I wake
up and I want to really

00:04:37.386 --> 00:04:39.196
want to go off and do that

00:04:39.196 --> 00:04:41.527
I'll often go out and do that
and cancel everything else

00:04:41.527 --> 00:04:43.060
that I was working on for that day.

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:45.101
Because chances are what
I create in that moment

00:04:45.101 --> 00:04:45.934
is going to be gold.

00:04:45.934 --> 00:04:47.851
Like when you're in the flow
and you're really feeling

00:04:47.851 --> 00:04:49.871
some thing what's going
to come out of that

00:04:49.871 --> 00:04:51.146
is going to be golden.

00:04:51.146 --> 00:04:52.942
The challenge is you're
not in the flow every day,

00:04:52.942 --> 00:04:54.989
at least me I'm not in flow every day.

00:04:54.989 --> 00:04:56.899
I don't wake up and flow I'm
just like a whole day of flow

00:04:56.899 --> 00:04:58.144
and I'm ready to go.

00:04:58.144 --> 00:05:00.831
That's not me, if that's you,
great, ignore this point.

00:05:00.831 --> 00:05:03.128
But most people don't
wake up and just flow

00:05:03.128 --> 00:05:03.986
the whole day.

00:05:03.986 --> 00:05:07.868
And so I had the routine for
when videos most of my days

00:05:07.868 --> 00:05:12.292
and then when I'm in flow I
go and follow that passion.

00:05:12.292 --> 00:05:15.652
At the same time when I feel like my

00:05:15.652 --> 00:05:17.817
something's missing or
feel like I want to add

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.594
something else to my schedule I mean

00:05:19.594 --> 00:05:20.914
something else has to be pulled out.

00:05:20.914 --> 00:05:23.124
And so whenever I feel like
the work that I'm doing

00:05:23.124 --> 00:05:26.407
in my calendar is not matching
up to what I want to do

00:05:26.407 --> 00:05:28.794
I have a vision, I have
dreams, I have other interests

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.182
I want to pursue.

00:05:30.182 --> 00:05:32.012
Then I start to change my schedule.

00:05:32.012 --> 00:05:34.630
So the schedule is what
I live by, it's what I

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:36.476
wake up and do on most days.

00:05:36.476 --> 00:05:39.521
And if I know it's in my
schedule it's going to get done.

00:05:39.521 --> 00:05:42.275
Super important because
left to my own devices

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:46.118
I would still be productive
but nowhere near as

00:05:46.118 --> 00:05:48.085
productive, nowehere near as disciplined.

00:05:48.085 --> 00:05:49.402
And so knowing what
you're going to do when

00:05:49.402 --> 00:05:51.354
you wake up but not having
to make choices on the side

00:05:51.354 --> 00:05:54.854
every single time makes life a lot easier.

00:05:56.996 --> 00:05:59.163
Tip number three is track your progress.

00:05:59.163 --> 00:06:01.250
There's a famous expression
that what gets measured

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.157
gets done or gets accomplished.

00:06:03.157 --> 00:06:06.040
When you are tracking what
you're doing you're more

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:09.049
likely to pay attention
to it and want to fix it.

00:06:09.049 --> 00:06:11.658
And so you know if your
goal is to lose weight

00:06:11.658 --> 00:06:13.771
if you're tracking your weight every day

00:06:13.771 --> 00:06:15.560
and you're tracking
your calories every day

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.347
you're much more likely to lose weight.

00:06:17.347 --> 00:06:19.857
You know if your goal is
to call 10 customers a day

00:06:19.857 --> 00:06:21.565
or reach out to ten people a day.

00:06:21.565 --> 00:06:23.987
Or you know make a
YouTube video every week

00:06:23.987 --> 00:06:26.012
if you are tracking it

00:06:26.012 --> 00:06:27.867
then you're more likely
to follow through on it.

00:06:27.867 --> 00:06:29.869
Just like when you're making
goals, the more specific

00:06:29.869 --> 00:06:32.354
you are the more likely
you're going to hit it.

00:06:32.354 --> 00:06:34.210
If your goal is to just lose weight

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:35.733
then you're unlikely to do it.

00:06:35.733 --> 00:06:37.285
But if your goal is to lose 10 pounds

00:06:37.285 --> 00:06:39.417
or 20 pounds, or your
goal is to hit you know

00:06:39.417 --> 00:06:42.238
$50,000 and more revenue
or whatever your goal is

00:06:42.238 --> 00:06:45.321
you're more likely to hit it
because you're being specific.

00:06:45.321 --> 00:06:47.417
And so if you're tracking
it on a daily basis

00:06:47.417 --> 00:06:50.502
or a weekly basis, then you
want to hit those numbers.

00:06:50.502 --> 00:06:53.915
You know when I'm working
out with my personal trainer

00:06:53.915 --> 00:06:55.932
you know he gives me goals I need to hit.

00:06:55.932 --> 00:06:59.475
Yeah I need to hit 900
calories a week in cardio

00:06:59.475 --> 00:07:00.921
as an example right now.

00:07:00.921 --> 00:07:03.661
So I have to do 45 minutes in two chunks

00:07:03.661 --> 00:07:07.420
45 minutes in 45 minutes
on the on the machine.

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:09.489
And I'm on social media is you
guys can check me out there

00:07:09.489 --> 00:07:11.570
when I'm answering your questions.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.796
Would I do 45 minutes without him?

00:07:13.796 --> 00:07:15.654
Maybe, maybe I'd do 15 minutes.

00:07:15.654 --> 00:07:17.383
Say, yeah okay, I'll do some cardio.

00:07:17.383 --> 00:07:19.373
Right but if you're
tracking it and you know

00:07:19.373 --> 00:07:21.585
it's happening and you make a
spreadsheet or use a checklist

00:07:21.585 --> 00:07:23.778
or whatever it is how you want to track

00:07:23.778 --> 00:07:25.958
don't get caught up in the
tools the tools don't matter.

00:07:25.958 --> 00:07:28.433
It could be a piece of paper
and a pen when you're checking

00:07:28.433 --> 00:07:30.164
something off and you
know you've got it done

00:07:30.164 --> 00:07:32.051
you're much more likely to follow through.

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:34.041
What gets tracked gets done.

00:07:34.041 --> 00:07:36.064
So anything you want
to stay disciplined on

00:07:36.064 --> 00:07:38.482
have some kind of
tracking system in place.

00:07:38.482 --> 00:07:41.511
Email or Evernote or a CRM or

00:07:41.511 --> 00:07:43.058
a calendar, anything.

00:07:43.058 --> 00:07:47.225
Something just so that you're
tracking it consistently.

00:07:49.763 --> 00:07:52.045
Tip number four is
commit to somebody else.

00:07:52.045 --> 00:07:53.945
When you commit to somebody
else you're much more likely

00:07:53.945 --> 00:07:54.855
to follow through.

00:07:54.855 --> 00:07:57.712
The reason is we will
let other people down

00:07:57.712 --> 00:08:00.076
less than we'll let ourselves down.

00:08:00.076 --> 00:08:01.652
It's easy to let ourselves down.

00:08:01.652 --> 00:08:05.009
How many times do we say
I'm going to do something

00:08:05.009 --> 00:08:06.308
but then you don't do it.

00:08:06.308 --> 00:08:08.272
You're letting yourself down right.

00:08:08.272 --> 00:08:09.105
Constantly.

00:08:09.105 --> 00:08:11.405
Even for you guys who snooze
I'm going to talk about that yet

00:08:11.405 --> 00:08:13.511
it's not on my list but let's go here now,

00:08:13.511 --> 00:08:15.285
don't snooze, stop
hitting the snooze button.

00:08:15.285 --> 00:08:17.503
The thing that happens when
you hit the snooze button is

00:08:17.503 --> 00:08:19.033
I'm going to wake up at 8:00 AM.

00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:20.456
Or I'm going to wake up at 7:00 AM

00:08:20.456 --> 00:08:22.603
and the first thing
you do is say that goal

00:08:22.603 --> 00:08:23.981
is not important to me.

00:08:23.981 --> 00:08:25.435
That's not going to happen.

00:08:25.435 --> 00:08:27.252
The first thing you do
every morning if you hit

00:08:27.252 --> 00:08:29.216
the snooze button is let yourself down.

00:08:29.216 --> 00:08:30.477
That's how you start your day.

00:08:30.477 --> 00:08:31.934
And if you hit the
snooze button five times

00:08:31.934 --> 00:08:35.964
you start your day every
day by letting yourself down

00:08:35.964 --> 00:08:37.474
five times.

00:08:37.474 --> 00:08:41.072
How well do you think that goes
for you to have a great day?

00:08:41.072 --> 00:08:42.408
Stop hitting the snooze button

00:08:42.408 --> 00:08:44.491
You're snoozing, you're
snoozing on everything,

00:08:44.491 --> 00:08:45.966
you're snoozing on your dreams,

00:08:45.966 --> 00:08:46.882
you're snoozing on your life.

00:08:46.882 --> 00:08:48.215
Stop it, get up.

00:08:49.365 --> 00:08:50.704
Back to the story.

00:08:50.704 --> 00:08:52.078
So when you commit to
somebody else you more

00:08:52.078 --> 00:08:53.687
likely to follow through.

00:08:53.687 --> 00:08:56.613
I do this in my work out
as an example you know

00:08:56.613 --> 00:08:59.787
I commit to my wife Nina and
Shawn our personal trainer

00:08:59.787 --> 00:09:02.471
that on Mondays and Wednesdays
we're going to work out.

00:09:02.471 --> 00:09:04.303
I'm there at five o'clock and we work out.

00:09:04.303 --> 00:09:07.584
If I'm feeling tired if I'm
feeling you know stressed out

00:09:07.584 --> 00:09:10.018
lots of work it's easy
to say you know what,

00:09:10.018 --> 00:09:11.608
I'm not going to do that,
that's not important.

00:09:11.608 --> 00:09:13.078
But because they're going to be there

00:09:13.078 --> 00:09:14.818
I'm going to be there.

00:09:14.818 --> 00:09:17.745
When I come in on Mondays
to work at Toronto here

00:09:17.745 --> 00:09:19.862
I work with Alex and I work with Lily

00:09:19.862 --> 00:09:21.116
and they're going to be
here and they're expecting

00:09:21.116 --> 00:09:23.580
me to be here we have a meeting set

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.460
and I have to go over stuff with them .

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:27.465
I have to show up I'm not
going to let them down.

00:09:27.465 --> 00:09:29.159
So whatever goal you have,
whatever you want to stay more

00:09:29.159 --> 00:09:32.406
disciplined with, try to
line up somebody to be with,

00:09:32.406 --> 00:09:35.135
try to line up a meeting
try, to line up a schedule.

00:09:35.135 --> 00:09:37.771
Try to line up something with
somebody else because if you

00:09:37.771 --> 00:09:41.938
commit to them you're more
likely to follow through.

00:09:43.435 --> 00:09:46.226
Tip number five is have
big whys and little whys.

00:09:46.226 --> 00:09:48.370
It's really important to
have a big why to feel like

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.204
what you're doing is
inspiring, is motivating.

00:09:50.204 --> 00:09:53.082
There's a reason for you
to get up and do work.

00:09:53.082 --> 00:09:55.991
If you feel like the work
you're doing is not important

00:09:55.991 --> 00:09:58.237
you're not going to
stay disciplined on it.

00:09:58.237 --> 00:10:00.045
If you feel like the work you're
doing is just pushing paper

00:10:00.045 --> 00:10:02.156
and just filling out forms and grunt work

00:10:02.156 --> 00:10:04.682
and administrative work, it's
something you don't care about

00:10:04.682 --> 00:10:06.253
you're not going to work hard.

00:10:06.253 --> 00:10:08.933
If you feel your work is
meaningless you don't want to

00:10:08.933 --> 00:10:10.293
work hard on that.

00:10:10.293 --> 00:10:12.217
It's really hard to say disciplined on it.

00:10:12.217 --> 00:10:14.430
And so having a big why and know that

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:16.870
the work that you're doing
matters, it means something

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:18.580
to people, you're working toward building

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:20.211
a better life for yourself.

00:10:20.211 --> 00:10:22.525
Whether you're thinking
about yourself and that

00:10:22.525 --> 00:10:24.010
ideal life you're trying to build

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.187
whether you think about
your family, your community

00:10:26.187 --> 00:10:27.603
or the customers you're serving

00:10:27.603 --> 00:10:29.133
having a big why helps you stay motivated.

00:10:29.133 --> 00:10:31.079
So for me I want to help
a billion entrepreneurs

00:10:31.079 --> 00:10:33.424
that's a big scary ambitious goal, right.

00:10:33.424 --> 00:10:35.015
Can I can I do it, is it possible?

00:10:35.015 --> 00:10:37.182
The work I do has meaning.

00:10:38.203 --> 00:10:40.887
I'm making these videos
trying to extend that goal.

00:10:40.887 --> 00:10:42.867
It's not just oh I've
got to fill more videos

00:10:42.867 --> 00:10:45.312
as soon as I get to that
point I'm done on YouTube.

00:10:45.312 --> 00:10:48.026
If I dread the thought of
coming in and making videos

00:10:48.026 --> 00:10:50.060
or if it's just okay like yeah whatever

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:51.250
got to go make some videos

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.206
I'm done, I have to move
on to something else.

00:10:53.206 --> 00:10:54.893
You have to do meaningful work.

00:10:54.893 --> 00:10:56.950
And so thinking about
what your big goal is,

00:10:56.950 --> 00:10:58.588
what your big vision is,

00:10:58.588 --> 00:11:00.027
the change you want to make

00:11:00.027 --> 00:11:02.719
and looking at that on a regular
basis, keeping that in mind

00:11:02.719 --> 00:11:05.051
and seeing how your work ties into you

00:11:05.051 --> 00:11:07.860
accomplishing that big
goal is really important.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:09.086
That's your big why.

00:11:09.086 --> 00:11:10.855
At the same time you have your little whys

00:11:10.855 --> 00:11:12.509
because the big why takes a long time.

00:11:12.509 --> 00:11:15.373
The big why is a lifetime goal right

00:11:15.373 --> 00:11:18.303
or a year goal or five year
like it it's out there,

00:11:18.303 --> 00:11:19.914
it's not going to happen today,

00:11:19.914 --> 00:11:21.177
it's not going to happen tomorrow.

00:11:21.177 --> 00:11:23.853
And so thinking long-term sometimes can

00:11:23.853 --> 00:11:26.109
be very motivating but
sometimes it can also

00:11:26.109 --> 00:11:29.884
bring you down sometimes it can also

00:11:29.884 --> 00:11:33.117
make you feel depressed like
I'm never going to hit that.

00:11:33.117 --> 00:11:34.762
Or, who am I to hit that big goal?

00:11:34.762 --> 00:11:36.849
I can't go out and do these big things.

00:11:36.849 --> 00:11:39.184
And so it doesn't always serve
you to the best that it can.

00:11:39.184 --> 00:11:41.045
And so that's why the little
whys are really important

00:11:41.045 --> 00:11:43.392
and the little whys are the
day-to-day little meanings

00:11:43.392 --> 00:11:45.215
that you have in your business.

00:11:45.215 --> 00:11:47.412
So for me is an example the big whys

00:11:47.412 --> 00:11:48.689
is helping a billion entrepreneurs.

00:11:48.689 --> 00:11:50.986
The little why are the
comments that you guys leave

00:11:50.986 --> 00:11:53.651
the little why is logging
everyday and seeing that

00:11:53.651 --> 00:11:55.949
you know Johnny really loved my video

00:11:55.949 --> 00:11:57.241
and it made a big impact.

00:11:57.241 --> 00:11:59.254
Like your comments mean a lot to me.

00:11:59.254 --> 00:12:02.690
I look at them every day it inspires me

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:03.631
and it inspires my team.

00:12:03.631 --> 00:12:06.829
And we know that yes we're
helping millions of people right

00:12:06.829 --> 00:12:09.473
we have millions of views
every month happening

00:12:09.473 --> 00:12:11.552
on the channel, we've had
over 100 million views

00:12:11.552 --> 00:12:12.540
on the channel.

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:15.436
It's numbers it's hard to even
imagine 100 million people

00:12:15.436 --> 00:12:17.539
watching these videos.

00:12:17.539 --> 00:12:21.321
But then to know that this
one person liked it and

00:12:21.321 --> 00:12:24.059
appreciated it and talked
about the impact that it had.

00:12:24.059 --> 00:12:26.354
Those day to day interactions
are really important.

00:12:26.354 --> 00:12:28.436
When I was first getting
started up in this business

00:12:28.436 --> 00:12:30.184
of helping entrepreneurs I would find

00:12:30.184 --> 00:12:32.136
this huge spike of enjoyment

00:12:32.136 --> 00:12:34.203
when I did I did speaking engagements.

00:12:34.203 --> 00:12:36.565
And I would speak and just feel so great.

00:12:36.565 --> 00:12:39.459
But it may be two weeks
until my next speaking gig

00:12:39.459 --> 00:12:41.319
and then in between I felt down like

00:12:41.319 --> 00:12:43.050
I didn't have anything like what,

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:44.443
I'm not getting any feedback,

00:12:44.443 --> 00:12:46.564
I don't know that my work is
meaningful or contributing.

00:12:46.564 --> 00:12:48.712
And so I would make a PowerPoint file

00:12:48.712 --> 00:12:50.458
that I would watch every morning

00:12:50.458 --> 00:12:53.013
and in it I would include
some of the feedback

00:12:53.013 --> 00:12:54.852
from the people who are in my sessions,

00:12:54.852 --> 00:12:56.434
some of the complimentary
things that people

00:12:56.434 --> 00:12:57.722
had to say for me to feel like yeah,

00:12:57.722 --> 00:13:00.281
the work I do is meaningful, it matters.

00:13:00.281 --> 00:13:02.528
And it's a little why it's
not solving a big problem,

00:13:02.528 --> 00:13:04.007
it's helping one person with one thing

00:13:04.007 --> 00:13:05.413
they had in their business.

00:13:05.413 --> 00:13:07.381
So I think that combination feeling like

00:13:07.381 --> 00:13:09.752
you're doing something
important on a big scale

00:13:09.752 --> 00:13:11.748
and also knowing that
the work you do today

00:13:11.748 --> 00:13:14.188
is touching one person's
life and have an impact

00:13:14.188 --> 00:13:18.355
it's easier much easier to
stay disciplined and on track.

00:13:20.709 --> 00:13:23.440
Tip number six is have
a designated workplace.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.205
This is really important
for entrepreneurs who

00:13:25.205 --> 00:13:26.686
are working from home.

00:13:26.686 --> 00:13:29.285
It can be hard when you have
all the comforts of your

00:13:29.285 --> 00:13:32.676
home to float in between and try to work

00:13:32.676 --> 00:13:34.736
in the kitchen and work on the couch

00:13:34.736 --> 00:13:37.663
and work from your bedroom or
wherever it is that you work.

00:13:37.663 --> 00:13:39.805
It can be hard to stay on task.

00:13:39.805 --> 00:13:42.231
It's easy to get distracted
by oh what's in the fridge.

00:13:42.231 --> 00:13:43.387
Oh what's on TV.

00:13:43.387 --> 00:13:44.804
Oh who's that calling.

00:13:44.804 --> 00:13:46.563
Oh the dog needs to be walked.

00:13:46.563 --> 00:13:48.382
They're all of the little
tasks that kind of come up

00:13:48.382 --> 00:13:49.436
and get you distracted.

00:13:49.436 --> 00:13:51.302
If you have an easy time seeing focus then

00:13:51.302 --> 00:13:52.827
it doesn't matter right

00:13:52.827 --> 00:13:54.542
it doesn't matter at all, you're fine.

00:13:54.542 --> 00:13:56.583
But you're not watching this video because

00:13:56.583 --> 00:13:57.941
you have a hard time staying disciplined

00:13:57.941 --> 00:13:58.774
and you want some tips.

00:13:58.774 --> 00:14:01.727
And so I would suggest having
designated place to work

00:14:01.727 --> 00:14:03.531
and also a designated time

00:14:03.531 --> 00:14:06.804
so that you know from nine AM to one PM

00:14:06.804 --> 00:14:08.840
you're going to work at this place.

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.996
And maybe that's outside the home,

00:14:10.996 --> 00:14:13.128
it could be leaving, it could
be going to a coffee shop

00:14:13.128 --> 00:14:15.051
or going to a library or going to a place

00:14:15.051 --> 00:14:17.414
of business somewhere that
you're going to go out there

00:14:17.414 --> 00:14:18.355
and work.

00:14:18.355 --> 00:14:21.035
Or it could be designated
spot and you know

00:14:21.035 --> 00:14:23.482
you have a home office in the
garage that you're setting up

00:14:23.482 --> 00:14:25.490
and when you're there you work.

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:27.469
And when you're not there
then you don't work.

00:14:27.469 --> 00:14:29.189
And I think that makes
it easier for people

00:14:29.189 --> 00:14:31.016
who have a hard time staying disciplined.

00:14:31.016 --> 00:14:33.293
You create a routine that
allows you to stay disciplined.

00:14:33.293 --> 00:14:36.470
So an example when Alex
and Lily both started

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:39.554
working for me and where I'm
helping mentor and coach them

00:14:39.554 --> 00:14:41.215
to become entrepreneurs

00:14:41.215 --> 00:14:44.781
I give them options like you
can either work from home,

00:14:44.781 --> 00:14:47.365
you can either work with
me, you can work from TDS,

00:14:47.365 --> 00:14:49.435
you can work from my place,
you can follow me around,

00:14:49.435 --> 00:14:51.684
you can whatever you want
to do whatever works best

00:14:51.684 --> 00:14:53.561
for your schedule, whatever works best

00:14:53.561 --> 00:14:55.082
for your personality style.

00:14:55.082 --> 00:14:57.782
And if they want to be
around me all the time

00:14:57.782 --> 00:14:59.933
and that helps going to keep consistency

00:14:59.933 --> 00:15:01.712
and like show up here
at nine o'clock great.

00:15:01.712 --> 00:15:03.437
If they want to work
from home or work from

00:15:03.437 --> 00:15:04.857
a coffee shop great.

00:15:04.857 --> 00:15:06.918
But creating a schedule
helps especially if

00:15:06.918 --> 00:15:08.465
you're not the discipline kind of person

00:15:08.465 --> 00:15:10.237
to know that you know Monday Tuesday

00:15:10.237 --> 00:15:11.941
Wednesday Thursday Friday Saturday

00:15:11.941 --> 00:15:13.936
whenever whatever days
you're working put it in.

00:15:13.936 --> 00:15:15.933
I have a designated place
that when I'm going here,

00:15:15.933 --> 00:15:18.260
I'm focused, I'm shutting
off all those distractions

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:19.593
and I'm working.

00:15:22.816 --> 00:15:25.396
And tip number seven is
do something you love.

00:15:25.396 --> 00:15:27.013
And this is the tip
that comes up most often

00:15:27.013 --> 00:15:28.525
when I look at famous entrepreneurs

00:15:28.525 --> 00:15:29.768
and how they achieve success.

00:15:29.768 --> 00:15:32.336
They did something that they love.

00:15:32.336 --> 00:15:34.074
If you are forcing
yourself to do something

00:15:34.074 --> 00:15:35.550
that you don't love you
can only do it for so long

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:36.761
before you're going to quit

00:15:36.761 --> 00:15:38.801
and want to give up and want
to move on something else.

00:15:38.801 --> 00:15:40.094
Because you don't love it.

00:15:40.094 --> 00:15:42.044
Not every day is amazing
as an entrepreneur

00:15:42.044 --> 00:15:45.164
but you have to actually
enjoy doing the work.

00:15:45.164 --> 00:15:47.521
Where if you sit down
and you're doing the work

00:15:47.521 --> 00:15:50.635
you don't see it as much
as being disciplined

00:15:50.635 --> 00:15:53.540
to have to do it because
you actually enjoy doing it.

00:15:53.540 --> 00:15:55.775
And so a lot of people
just set these big goals

00:15:55.775 --> 00:15:57.629
for themselves and they'll
do whatever it takes

00:15:57.629 --> 00:15:59.098
to go up and get there.

00:15:59.098 --> 00:16:01.602
But if they don't actually
enjoy the process of doing it

00:16:01.602 --> 00:16:03.819
they're never going to actually go out

00:16:03.819 --> 00:16:05.135
and achieve those goals.

00:16:05.135 --> 00:16:07.953
Much more important is that
the work that you're doing

00:16:07.953 --> 00:16:09.454
is something that you
are passionate about.

00:16:09.454 --> 00:16:10.655
There has to be something in your business

00:16:10.655 --> 00:16:11.561
that you can get lost in.

00:16:11.561 --> 00:16:12.676
There has to be.

00:16:12.676 --> 00:16:14.211
If everything is just work to you

00:16:14.211 --> 00:16:15.251
you're not going to make it.

00:16:15.251 --> 00:16:16.496
Like quit now and go do something else

00:16:16.496 --> 00:16:17.867
that you can get lost in.

00:16:17.867 --> 00:16:19.468
Not every piece of your
business you're going

00:16:19.468 --> 00:16:21.089
to be able to get lost in
especially at the beginning

00:16:21.089 --> 00:16:23.286
because you're doing everything.

00:16:23.286 --> 00:16:25.585
And you may not get lost in
the accounting of your business

00:16:25.585 --> 00:16:28.022
maybe you love accounting
and that's great.

00:16:28.022 --> 00:16:29.172
Be an accountant.

00:16:29.172 --> 00:16:31.056
But otherwise a lot of
people don't want to do the

00:16:31.056 --> 00:16:33.228
accounting side or don't want
to care about their taxes

00:16:33.228 --> 00:16:34.265
and all that kind of stuff.

00:16:34.265 --> 00:16:35.794
It has to get done.

00:16:35.794 --> 00:16:37.869
But there has to be
something in your business

00:16:37.869 --> 00:16:41.333
that you can get lost in
and forget what time it is.

00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:43.908
And the more you're
doing that kind of work

00:16:43.908 --> 00:16:45.654
the more you're going
to be able to not just

00:16:45.654 --> 00:16:47.790
stay disciplined but
achieve your big goals.

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:49.945
And as soon as possible
I've been looking at

00:16:49.945 --> 00:16:52.769
how can I build a team to
be able to take away some

00:16:52.769 --> 00:16:55.243
of the things that I don't
like that I keep getting

00:16:55.243 --> 00:16:57.439
drawn in by or keep procrastinating.

00:16:57.439 --> 00:16:59.478
And give that to somebody
else so I can focus on

00:16:59.478 --> 00:17:01.077
what I can be great at.

00:17:01.077 --> 00:17:03.701
So those are my seven tips on
how to stay more disciplined.

00:17:03.701 --> 00:17:05.717
I'd love to know what do you guys think.

